<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Android 17 overlay on the base manifest (LineageOS lineage-24.0, or stock AOSP
  android-17.0.0_r1), for syncs that track branch heads instead of the pin: the weekly image job's
  refresh, and any build with "Pin to Remora's tested manifest" unticked.

  KEEP IT IN STEP WITH pinned-manifest-a17.xml. That one is the reproducible pin and this is the
  tip-tracking overlay, so a project present in only one of them makes the build depend on which
  manifest was used. The weekly job refuses a refresh that loses a project the pin has; that
  refusal is how the entry below was found missing (bd remora-q6t5).

  ONE PROJECT. external/intel-media-driver builds iHD_drv_video.so, the VA driver that every
  hardware video path goes through. AOSP deleted the project in Android 17 and nothing replaces
  it, so the pin carries the Android 16 revision across releases (bd remora-28ix.7), and this file
  must too. Without it a refreshed tree has no VA driver and the build does not fail: the module is
  simply undefined. The intel_media_driver_dri_path source patch fixes where the driver installs.

  Never deleted, even when it lists no projects, because the engine requires it to exist.
  SourceBuild.cpp's unpinned path does
  `cp <source-build>/local_manifests/remora-a<ver>*.xml .repo/local_manifests/` and Chain.cpp
  preflights the glob, so removing the file breaks unpinned A17 builds with a missing-manifest
  error rather than doing nothing. It was empty from R3 (bd remora-ykhz), which retired the last
  upstream prebuilts project by building Mesa from source, until the entry below.

  Everything Remora authors — device/remora, vendor/remora, hardware/remora/c2-va — is
  deliberately NOT a project here and never was. It is vendored under vendor/source-build/ and
  staged into the tree before lunch. No manifest can provide Remora-authored source, and pointing
  a remote at one machine's disk made the build unreproducible everywhere else (bd remora-28ix.4).

  The upstream device tree and its OMX and c2 components were removed in R2c (bd
  remora-28ix.4): A17 lunches the staged device/remora, the codec2 wiring is absorbed into
  vendor/remora, and the OMX plugin gated on a boot arg Remora never emitted.

  Base tree:  repo init -u https://github.com/LineageOS/android.git -b lineage-24.0
  or AOSP:    repo init -u https://android.googlesource.com/platform/manifest -b android-17.0.0_r1
  Lunch:      remora_x86_64-cp2a-userdebug
  See bead remora-cbd.
-->
<manifest>
  <project name="platform/external/intel-media-driver" path="external/intel-media-driver"
           remote="aosp" revision="refs/tags/android-16.0.0_r1" groups="pdk" />
</manifest>
